{
  "id": "lebesgue-measure-oq-06-oq-01",
  "name": "Hausdorff free subgroup theorem in SO(3) formalized in Lean",
  "status": "completed",
  "phase": "COMPLETED",
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "The parent (lebesgue-measure-oq-06) already proves Hausdorff's free subgroup theorem, but states injectivity of FreeGroup.lift through the underlying linear equivalences (≃ₗ), forgetting that the generators are isometries. The genuinely new content is to realise the embedding internally to the isometry group ℝ³ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℝ³ and package it as group theory uses it.",
      "Freeness is stable under any faithful homomorphism: e ↦ e.toLinearEquiv is an injective group hom O(3) →* GL(ℝ³), and injectivity of a homomorphism out of F₂ is detected after composing with it. So the parent's lift into ≃ₗ factoring as toLinearEquivHom ∘ (lift into ≃ₗᵢ) transfers injectivity back into the isometry group with no orbit argument reproved.",
      "The forgetful map is a monoid hom precisely because both groups M ≃ₗ[R] M and M ≃ₗᵢ[R] M use the same composition convention a * b = b.trans a; multiplicativity is then exactly LinearIsometryEquiv.toLinearEquiv_trans, and MonoidHom.mk' needs only map_mul.",
      "'SO(3) contains a copy of F₂' is exactly MonoidHom.ofInjective applied to the free embedding: an injective hom is the same data as an isomorphism FreeGroup Bool ≃* f.range onto a subgroup.",
      "Non-abelianness comes for free: two distinct free generators never commute (proved decidably via a map to S₃ = Perm (Fin 3)), and this transfers along the injective hom to give two explicit non-commuting rotations.",
      "Axiom hygiene: the file imports the parent (which declares the axiom banach_tarski for the full ball decomposition), but #print axioms confirms every result depends only on the fully-proved hausdorff_free_subgroup plus propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound — 0 axioms, no sorryAx, no Lean.ofReduceBool (decide is kernel reduction)."
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "BanachTarski.toLinearEquivHom (Proofs/LebesgueMeasureOQ06OQ01.lean:69) — forgetful monoid hom (ℝ³ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℝ³) →* (ℝ³ ≃ₗ[ℝ] ℝ³)",
      "BanachTarski.hausdorff_free_subgroup_isometry (:88) — FreeGroup.lift into the isometry group ℝ³ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℝ³ is injective (Hausdorff's theorem internal to O(3))",
      "BanachTarski.isometryGroup_contains_freeGroup (:109) — an injective group hom FreeGroup Bool →* (ℝ³ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℝ³)",
      "BanachTarski.exists_freeGroup_mulEquiv_rotationSubgroup (:119) — a subgroup S with FreeGroup Bool ≃* S; SO(3) contains a literal copy of F₂",
      "BanachTarski.freeGroup_of_true_false_ne (:128) — the two generators of FreeGroup Bool do not commute (decidable via S₃)",
      "BanachTarski.exists_noncommuting_rotations (:144) — two non-commuting rotations of ℝ³; SO(3) is non-abelian"
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Show the generators have determinant +1 to place the free subgroup in SO(3) (special orthogonal) rather than merely O(3) at the Lean level.",
      "Derive non-amenability of the isometry group directly: any group containing F₂ is non-amenable, closing the chain to the parent's free_group_not_amenable.",
      "Transport the free group's paradoxical decomposition along the embedding to a paradoxical decomposition of S² minus a countable set (the full Hausdorff paradox)."
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: Hausdorff's free subgroup of SO(3) realised internally to the isometry group ℝ³ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℝ³ — forgetful bridge toLinearEquivHom, injective free embedding FreeGroup Bool →* O(3), isomorphic subgroup FreeGroup Bool ≃* S, and explicit non-commuting rotations. 6 theorems / 1 def, verified 0 sorries / 0 axioms (only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound; no result depends on the parent's banach_tarski axiom). Verified offline via lake env lean against the parent's axiom-stubbed lemma with explicit Mathlib imports (EXIT 0, #print axioms clean); docker down so full import build deferred to CI. PR opened."
  },
